# Source files are stored and checked out as LF. Without this, Windows autocrlf=true commits CRLF
# blobs that the Linux CI ruff-format / cargo-fmt gates reject (the v1.13.46 main.py line-ending
# incident). eol=lf also stops the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" working-tree churn on Windows.
*.py text eol=lf
*.rs text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles MUST be LF, and this is a correctness requirement, not style:
# a CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` fails inside a Linux container with `bad interpreter: No such file
# or directory`, and a CRLF Dockerfile line can carry a stray \r into an ENV value. Added with
# scripts/ci-local/ (the local CI-parity harness), whose scripts run only inside a Linux container.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
